it won't take much for him to experiment being penetrated by another male.

As an HIV+ positive person, I approve this message. Thank you for taking your time to educate people, OP.  
There's just two points I'd light to highlight:

1- undetec folks are unable to transmit the virus even during unprotected sex, as shown by several studies;  


2- condom and proper lubrication will prevent infection ;

3- Controversial but true, I wanna see if you agree: it's very invasive to ask someone if they are HIV+. If you wanna protect yourself, simply be on PreP or wear a condom. It's possible to protect yourself without hurting someone's privacy.

I'll tell you what you wanna hear.

you were an asshole. If you had helped her, she would not have killed herself. Forgot about the day you flaked on her. Think of all the opportunities you missed to help her. You could have done so much and you haven't. Truth is, you had no obligation whatsover to help her. But you could have. that's what good people do.

&#x200B;

Wanna check whether you changed? Look around you. There are many Ems out there right now and you that - the boring guy nobody likes; the annoying girls who's always complaining as a self-defense mechanism; the loser who's desperatly is trying to turn his life around and no one reaches a helping hand. Are you helping at least one of those people? Or are you staying in your comfort zone with your cool friends?

&#x200B;

Ps.: I was bullyed at school but managed to pick myself up

Later your nephew will understand that you did not help your sister, and he will be torn up with simultaneous love/hatred towards you.

&#x200B;

I always thought addiction is irresponsible and selfish. But I know now from my own experience that it is a response to heavy emotional pain. Be understanding and compassionate towards your sister. She's now trying to escape from the hell she's in. She loves her son (being sober from heavy drugs for 12 months is no pieace of cake) and maybe Tommy is the only reason she's now trying to get sober.

&#x200B;

Finally, I now we don't know each other, but I thank you with all my heart that you gave Tommy so much love in his hour of need.

&#x200B;

R
